# Commit messages (Generate Commit Message + agents)

When generating a Git commit message for this repository, follow **Conventional Commits** exactly.

## Format

```
<type>(<scope>): <subject>

[optional body]
```

- **One subject line** only by default (≤72 characters).
- Subject: imperative mood, lowercase after the colon, **no trailing period**.
- Focus on **why** / outcome — not a file list or diff restatement.
- Body: only if needed; short bullets; wrap ~72 chars.
- Language: **English** for type/scope/subject (matches code identifiers).

## Types (pick one)

| type | when |
|------|------|
| `feat` | new user-facing capability |
| `fix` | bug fix |
| `refactor` | change structure, same behavior |
| `docs` | docs / comments only |
| `style` | formatting, no logic change |
| `test` | tests only |
| `chore` | tooling, deps, config, housekeeping |
| `perf` | performance |
| `build` | build system / bundler |

## Scope (optional but preferred)

Short area: `study`, `words`, `import`, `api`, `db`, `ui`, `deploy`.

## Do not

- Do not use `Updated files`, `Various changes`, or vague subjects.
- Do not paste a changelog of every file.
- Do not wrap the whole message in markdown fences or quotes.
